Subject: [PATCH] fix(auction): confirm visible response cards and sync countdown

Optional hardening after the viewed-only fix. The server claim remains the
source of truth; this only prevents off-screen cards from starting the timer
and makes the UI reflect the successful claim immediately.

--- a/src/components/auction/ManagerColumn.tsx
+++ b/src/components/auction/ManagerColumn.tsx
@@
  const isMounted = useIsMounted();
@@
- useEffect(() => {
- if (!isCurrentUser || state.response_deadline !== null) return;
+ useEffect(() => {
+ if (!isCurrentUser || state.response_deadline !== null) return;
+ const element = document.querySelector(`[data-response-auction-id="${state.auction_id}"]`);
+ if (!(element instanceof HTMLElement)) return;
+ const observer = new IntersectionObserver(async ([entry]) => {
+   if (!entry.isIntersecting || entry.intersectionRatio < 0.5) return;
+   observer.disconnect();
+   const response = await fetch(`/api/leagues/${leagueId}/players/${state.player_id}/response-timer/viewed`, { method: "POST" });
+   if (!response.ok) return;
+   const result = await response.json() as { deadline?: number };
+   // Feed result.deadline into the parent state/store so the countdown starts
+   // immediately instead of waiting for the next polling response.
+ }, { threshold: [0.5] });
+ observer.observe(element);
+ return () => observer.disconnect();
+ }, [isCurrentUser, leagueId, state.auction_id, state.player_id, state.response_deadline]);
*** End Patch
